WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.200 --> 00:01.880
- You ditched work to listen to Dr. Pun again

3
00:02.160 --> 00:03.640
- You can’t keep living like this.

4
00:03.920 --> 00:05.200
- Are you still playing Cupid?

5
00:05.440 --> 00:06.000
- Hello.

6
00:06.080 --> 00:07.240
- Are you Mr. Monsieur?

7
00:07.320 --> 00:08.240
- You’re here for the blind date, too?

8
00:08.360 --> 00:10.720
- I’ll show you how many matches I get.

9
00:11.280 --> 00:13.120
- Are you sure you don’t want to rank anyone?

10
00:13.520 --> 00:14.560
- What are you doing, Dean?

11
00:14.560 --> 00:15.680
- Are you trying to match with everyone?

12
00:15.680 --> 00:18.040
- I believe in equality.

13
00:20.080 --> 00:21.960
- [SURFING DOLPHIN]

14
00:24.960 --> 00:27.080
- [SURFING DOLPHIN, NUMBER OF MATCHES: 1]

15
01:49.960 --> 01:52.320
[SPICY PORK BACKBONE SOUP]

16
02:14.880 --> 02:16.920
So we just put these on and dig in?

17
02:27.400 --> 02:30.280
Whoa. They’re huge.

18
02:32.680 --> 02:33.960
You said there were bones and chilies.

19
02:35.079 --> 02:35.960
Why do you want to eat this?

20
02:37.360 --> 02:38.560
Well, I want to try it.

21
02:39.320 --> 02:40.200
Ever heard of ‘being open-minded’?

22
02:45.280 --> 02:46.040
What’s wrong with you?

23
02:46.640 --> 02:47.640
When I disagree with you, you get mad.

24
02:48.400 --> 02:49.680
When I spoil you, you pick a fight.

25
03:02.240 --> 03:05.320
Hmm, it’s pretty good.

26
03:08.200 --> 03:09.280
Are you trying to comfort me?

27
03:12.280 --> 03:13.120
No, it’s actually good.

28
03:31.720 --> 03:32.240
Okay.

29
03:33.440 --> 03:35.480
Do I like it? No.

30
03:36.800 --> 03:40.440
But now that I’ve tried it, I get why you like it.

31
03:48.160 --> 03:49.200
Here, eat.

32
04:18.440 --> 04:19.480
Hot and spicy as always.

33
04:22.480 --> 04:23.400
Feeling better now?

34
04:26.400 --> 04:26.840
Why?

35
04:27.840 --> 04:30.200
Is it so obvious that I’m in a terrible mood?

36
04:31.560 --> 04:32.120
No.

37
04:33.680 --> 04:38.840
But they say eating something you like makes you feel better.

38
04:39.760 --> 04:42.520
So you’re spoiling me because you think I’m upset?

39
04:43.480 --> 04:44.800
That’s why you brought me here, right?

40
04:47.320 --> 04:48.159
What else could I do?

41
04:48.760 --> 04:50.040
We matched, so I have to stick with you.

42
04:51.159 --> 04:51.840
Those are the rules.

43
04:53.120 --> 04:54.760
I couldn’t stand spending time with someone moody,

44
04:55.320 --> 04:56.760
I couldn’t stand spending time with someone moody,

45
04:57.760 --> 04:58.240
No way.

46
05:11.560 --> 05:12.160
Thank you…

47
05:15.800 --> 05:16.480
for taking pity on me.

48
05:22.320 --> 05:23.360
What’s there to pity?

49
05:24.800 --> 05:26.520
You just didn’t get matched with anyone else

50
05:28.280 --> 05:28.800
but me.

51
05:31.480 --> 05:31.920
That.

52
05:34.000 --> 05:34.560
Thank you.

53
05:40.440 --> 05:41.880
Eat up. Isn’t this your favorite?

54
06:14.560 --> 06:15.200
I forgot.

55
06:15.200 --> 06:17.240
(Oh, come on!)

56
06:17.600 --> 06:18.760
(That’s your excuse?)

57
06:18.760 --> 06:20.320
(You’ve been getting smoother every day, jackass.)

58
06:21.000 --> 06:21.640
Sorry.

59
06:22.160 --> 06:22.840
I’m sorry, Jo.

60
06:23.440 --> 06:24.960
You’ve never been like this, dude.

61
06:25.160 --> 06:27.040
I opened a new club,

62
06:27.480 --> 06:28.960
(and you haven’t come by even once.)

63
06:28.960 --> 06:30.400
(Jo said it himself.)

64
06:30.400 --> 06:32.000
(You gotta come.)

65
06:32.760 --> 06:33.920
I have plans with Moth.

66
06:34.440 --> 06:36.080
(There it is. My guess is never wrong.)

67
06:36.640 --> 06:38.320
(Being with your special someone is fine,)

68
06:38.600 --> 06:40.440
(but you gotta make time for your friends too, man.)

69
06:41.440 --> 06:42.480
Hey, I gotta go.

70
06:57.480 --> 06:58.159
Did I keep you waiting?

71
06:59.159 --> 06:59.760
Yeah.

72
07:00.480 --> 07:01.200
Sorry.

73
07:01.720 --> 07:02.440
Come on in.

74
07:14.000 --> 07:14.800
What were you doing?

75
07:16.360 --> 07:17.240
What took you so long?

76
07:18.120 --> 07:18.880
I was on the phone.

77
07:19.440 --> 07:22.800
Ohm and Boom asked if I wanted to go to Jo’s new club.

78
07:23.840 --> 07:24.400
I knew it.

79
07:25.640 --> 07:26.560
It’s Friday night.

80
07:27.600 --> 07:28.240
Aren’t you going out?

81
07:29.000 --> 07:29.480
No.

82
07:30.760 --> 07:32.200
I want to stay in with you.

83
07:34.520 --> 07:34.800
Ouch.

84
07:35.800 --> 07:38.200
Ouch, that hurts.

85
07:38.400 --> 07:39.080
So dramatic.

86
07:40.520 --> 07:41.400
I meant I want to get inside the house.

87
07:41.600 --> 07:42.760
What are you thinking?

88
07:43.400 --> 07:44.640
I’m not having dirty thoughts like you..

89
07:48.840 --> 07:49.360
[5 G-CH 203, BANGKOK]

90
07:51.640 --> 07:52.480
Do you usually drive?

91
07:53.400 --> 07:54.240
I’ve never seen you drive.

92
07:55.880 --> 07:58.240
Bangkok traffic is horrible. I get frustrated on the road.

93
07:58.720 --> 07:59.159
Why?

94
08:00.080 --> 08:02.320
Wanna be my passenger princess?

95
08:03.720 --> 08:04.600
What kind of joke is that?

96
08:05.280 --> 08:05.880
Lame.

97
08:24.880 --> 08:26.480
Do you really live alone?

98
08:28.400 --> 08:28.840
Why?

99
08:30.040 --> 08:32.880
It looks like you live with your mom.

100
08:34.440 --> 08:35.400
I do live alone.

101
08:35.760 --> 08:37.240
My older sister comes to visit from time to time.

102
08:37.640 --> 08:39.200
My parents barely ever come by.

103
08:41.720 --> 08:42.080
Why?

104
08:43.400 --> 08:44.360
Is it hard to believe?

105
08:46.240 --> 08:46.760
Well?

106
08:47.560 --> 08:48.320
What are you cooking for me?

107
08:53.520 --> 08:56.120
What do you feel like eating?

108
09:08.400 --> 09:08.840
Hey.

109
09:10.960 --> 09:12.000
You asked me over for food.

110
09:12.360 --> 09:13.040
So let’s eat food.

111
09:23.120 --> 09:25.720
Did you steal a restaurant’s fridge?

112
09:27.720 --> 09:28.280
What?

113
09:29.960 --> 09:31.520
Come on. What an exaggeration.

114
09:36.120 --> 09:38.640
Hey, we’ve got some chuck.

115
09:39.920 --> 09:40.800
How about steak?

116
09:41.680 --> 09:42.320
Mm.

117
09:47.200 --> 09:48.640
What’s this?

118
09:49.000 --> 09:50.000
Snakeskin gourami?

119
09:50.000 --> 09:51.400
Yeah. Why?

120
09:52.000 --> 09:52.640
Want some?

121
09:54.000 --> 09:55.560
Straight from a premium farm.

122
09:58.280 --> 10:00.240
What are these?

123
10:01.040 --> 10:01.880
Stocks.

124
10:02.240 --> 10:03.880
Kombu stock and chicken stock.

125
10:04.240 --> 10:05.280
I make them whenever I have time.

126
10:05.720 --> 10:06.600
Saves time when I wanna cook.

127
10:09.880 --> 10:10.800
Who the heck are you?

128
10:12.800 --> 10:13.360
All set.

129
10:21.880 --> 10:22.520
Need some help?

130
10:24.800 --> 10:25.720
Make a salad.

131
10:27.280 --> 10:27.760
Sure.

132
10:53.240 --> 10:55.480
Oh, there’s some cos lettuce in the fridge.

133
10:55.800 --> 10:56.560
You can add that too.

134
10:58.360 --> 10:59.520
What’s cos lettuce?

135
11:00.280 --> 11:01.080
Are you serious?

136
11:03.760 --> 11:04.560
Hold this for a sec.

137
11:09.080 --> 11:11.200
This is cos lettuce.

138
11:13.800 --> 11:14.760
I thought it was called salad veggie.

139
11:17.040 --> 11:20.400
If you’re gonna call it that, just call it lettuce.

140
11:22.000 --> 11:22.360
Ouch.

141
11:24.240 --> 11:25.240
It’s splattering!

142
11:28.120 --> 11:28.520
Hold on.

143
11:31.960 --> 11:32.360
Here.

144
11:59.080 --> 12:00.960
Abracadabra! All better now.

145
12:12.040 --> 12:13.400
Go have a seat.

146
12:14.200 --> 12:16.760
Chef Dean will take care of everything.

147
13:09.360 --> 13:10.200
Have a bite.

148
13:23.040 --> 13:24.240
How is it? Good?

149
13:28.520 --> 13:29.240
Pretty good.

150
13:30.600 --> 13:32.520
Pretty good? Meaning?

151
13:33.800 --> 13:36.800
Pretty good means delicious.

152
13:42.120 --> 13:45.400
Will you stay over tonight?

153
13:49.280 --> 13:50.280
Let me think about it.

154
14:10.960 --> 14:14.160
You did a big cleanup to welcome me?

155
14:14.640 --> 14:15.880
It always looks like this.

156
14:26.800 --> 14:27.560
Can I have that back?

157
14:28.160 --> 14:28.960
Forgot to put it away.

158
14:44.280 --> 14:45.840
How many people have been in this room?

159
14:47.520 --> 14:48.280
Have you ever counted?

160
14:48.520 --> 14:49.960
I’ve never brought anyone here.

161
14:52.760 --> 14:53.320
Hey, I’m serious.

162
14:57.360 --> 15:00.080
So I’m the first?

163
15:04.160 --> 15:04.760
Mm.

164
15:06.960 --> 15:12.080
I may babble a lot, but I’m telling the truth this time.

165
15:13.720 --> 15:14.880
I’m not lying.

166
15:16.440 --> 15:20.720
You’re the first person I’ve ever brought into my room.

167
15:38.320 --> 15:39.640
I can swear to it if you want.

168
15:50.680 --> 15:52.280
I never said I didn’t believe you.

169
16:31.160 --> 16:31.960
Is the tee comfy enough?

170
16:33.360 --> 16:34.520
Yeah, it is.

171
16:36.600 --> 16:37.680
If it’s too tight, I’ll get you a new one.

172
16:40.600 --> 16:44.160
Why does it say ‘Love’ here, not ‘Live’?

173
16:45.480 --> 16:46.800
They printed it wrong.

174
16:47.600 --> 16:51.240
So it’s more special than the others.

175
16:59.120 --> 17:02.080
Sit back and relax. Let me take care of you.

176
17:46.000 --> 17:46.600
Hey.

177
17:51.160 --> 17:51.720
Dean.

178
18:03.560 --> 18:04.360
I can’t sleep.

179
18:07.400 --> 18:08.200
Is it too cold?

180
18:13.240 --> 18:16.320
Or… is the mattress too soft?

181
18:18.520 --> 18:18.880
No.

182
18:21.920 --> 18:22.840
I’m just not used to it.

183
18:24.080 --> 18:25.440
I’m more comfortable in my own room.

184
18:26.760 --> 18:29.120
Can I go home?

185
18:33.080 --> 18:33.600
Okay.

186
18:33.720 --> 18:35.320
I’ll book you a ride.

187
18:38.800 --> 18:41.880
It’s okay. I can do it.

188
19:09.600 --> 19:11.160
[I’M HOME.]

189
19:18.640 --> 19:20.160
[SWEET DREAMS.]

190
19:28.640 --> 19:30.560
[I’M SORRY.]

191
19:37.120 --> 19:39.720
[IT’S ALL GOOD. WASH THE TEE, THOUGH.]

192
20:18.720 --> 20:19.120
Yeah?

193
20:19.360 --> 20:20.240
(Morning.)

194
20:20.400 --> 20:21.280
Going anywhere today?

195
20:21.440 --> 20:22.120
Staying in.

196
20:22.280 --> 20:23.160
Got some work to do.

197
20:24.120 --> 20:25.360
Where will you go after that?

198
20:25.480 --> 20:27.520
I’ve got a Zoom meeting with a new client.

199
20:27.680 --> 20:29.280
I don’t know when we’ll wrap up—

200
20:29.280 --> 20:30.160
Hi, Moth.

201
20:30.560 --> 20:32.280
Can we borrow Dean for a sec for some content?

202
20:32.720 --> 20:34.560
Hey, are you guys working?

203
20:35.000 --> 20:36.280
(Then get to work.)

204
20:37.400 --> 20:38.000
I’m hanging up.

205
20:45.480 --> 20:45.800
Hey.

206
20:46.280 --> 20:47.640
Why the hell did you two have to show up now?

207
20:49.080 --> 20:51.080
It’s been so hard to see you lately.

208
20:51.400 --> 20:52.000
You’re so clingy to your boyfriend.

209
20:52.000 --> 20:53.120
Moth and I aren’t boyfriends.

210
20:53.280 --> 20:54.520
Oh, really?

211
20:54.720 --> 20:57.880
But you two are acting more like a couple than we do.

212
20:58.400 --> 20:58.800
Oops.

213
21:00.120 --> 21:02.240
But our couple is still the best.

214
21:02.600 --> 21:04.560
Aww, are you sulking?

215
21:04.600 --> 21:07.080
There, there.

216
21:07.080 --> 21:07.920
There.

217
21:10.040 --> 21:11.640
(I just saw your status, Mr. Bagel.)

218
21:11.920 --> 21:13.480
(Any updates for us?)

219
21:14.680 --> 21:15.480
It’s nothing.

220
21:16.120 --> 21:17.600
I just posted it for good luck.

221
21:18.160 --> 21:20.720
And I’m just hoping something good comes my way.

222
21:21.960 --> 21:23.600
(Is it about the blind date thing you went to?)

223
21:24.040 --> 21:25.080
(Do we have some good news?)

224
21:25.720 --> 21:28.480
If you mean him, then no. We’re not talking anymore.

225
21:29.720 --> 21:32.800
Actually, you can ask Mr. Monsieur too.

226
21:32.800 --> 21:35.080
He also went to the blind date event.

227
21:40.280 --> 21:40.800
I…

228
21:41.400 --> 21:44.600
I didn’t see or talk to anyone.

229
21:45.200 --> 21:47.880
I… had to rush home.

230
21:47.880 --> 21:49.280
(What a shame.)

231
21:49.640 --> 21:52.040
(I thought Mr. Bagel and Mr. Monsieur might get to meet.)

232
21:55.280 --> 21:57.640
Anyway, is everyone coming to the Good Boi Party?

233
21:57.800 --> 21:59.320
You guys aren’t bailing on me, are you?

234
21:59.320 --> 22:00.800
(Of course we’re coming.)

235
22:00.880 --> 22:04.480
(I’m about to prepare crispy chicken for everyone’s pup.)

236
22:06.400 --> 22:07.000
Come, come.

237
22:07.440 --> 22:09.640
I want to meet you all.

238
22:12.880 --> 22:14.760
It sounds fun.

239
22:16.640 --> 22:17.600
Right?

240
22:18.240 --> 22:21.840
You’re not gonna back out on me, are you, Mr. Monsieur?

241
22:23.440 --> 22:26.760
If we don’t get to meet, I’m seriously going to be mad at you.

242
22:34.520 --> 22:35.800
What should Daddy do, baby girl?

243
22:53.360 --> 22:53.680
Here.

244
22:57.800 --> 22:58.440
What did I tell you?

245
22:58.840 --> 23:00.840
Wow, you should see your face.

246
23:00.840 --> 23:02.120
Here you go, as ordered, sir.

247
23:15.960 --> 23:18.120
Is this the client you’re designing a mascot for?

248
23:18.480 --> 23:19.960
They didn’t give me much to work with.

249
23:20.560 --> 23:21.160
Just this photo.

250
23:22.320 --> 23:22.920
Isn’t that good?

251
23:23.520 --> 23:25.800
You can sell any idea.

252
23:27.960 --> 23:28.720
Who told you that?

253
23:29.320 --> 23:31.720
Any job with no clear brief is the hardest.

254
23:32.000 --> 23:33.560
Have you been to this place?

255
23:36.520 --> 23:37.520
No, I haven’t.

256
23:38.600 --> 23:40.320
I think I’ll have to make time to go there.

257
23:41.520 --> 23:45.800
I can’t really picture it from just one photo.

258
23:45.880 --> 23:46.600
How are you getting there?

259
23:46.960 --> 23:48.120
Do you know the way?

260
23:51.120 --> 23:53.920
I guess I’ll take a van.

261
23:56.960 --> 23:57.960
Sounds like a hassle.

262
23:59.600 --> 24:02.320
What else can I do? I don’t have a car.

263
24:04.280 --> 24:05.160
What about my car?

264
24:06.920 --> 24:07.440
What?

265
24:08.800 --> 24:09.480
Are you offering to drive me?

266
24:09.960 --> 24:14.240
We’ve never taken a trip out of town together.

267
24:51.720 --> 24:52.200
Moth.

268
24:53.080 --> 24:53.720
Pose for the photos.

269
24:56.440 --> 24:57.200
Wanna get on that?

270
25:50.000 --> 25:50.480
Here.

271
26:24.840 --> 26:25.920
Let’s go to this café after.

272
26:26.960 --> 26:27.880
Tons of good reviews.

273
26:28.480 --> 26:29.960
Oh, let’s not.

274
26:30.600 --> 26:31.760
Those are all paid reviews.

275
26:31.760 --> 26:33.200
I doubt the actual place is as nice as the pictures.

276
26:33.800 --> 26:34.560
Don’t go there.

277
26:35.720 --> 26:37.200
Nice or not, I can decide for myself.

278
26:37.280 --> 26:39.640
You have to see it for yourself to tell.

279
26:40.520 --> 26:41.320
No.

280
26:42.040 --> 26:43.960
It’s too far, and it’s not on our way.

281
26:44.480 --> 26:45.480
Yes, it is.

282
26:45.680 --> 26:46.160
Look.

283
26:50.840 --> 26:51.560
What?

284
26:52.280 --> 26:53.680
What’s stopping you from going?

285
26:54.840 --> 26:55.880
Is your ex-lover there?

286
26:55.880 --> 26:57.200
No. There’s nothing there.

287
26:57.760 --> 26:59.240
If you want to go, let’s go.

288
27:24.080 --> 27:24.960
Just admit it.

289
27:25.280 --> 27:26.680
Do you have a fling living around here?

290
27:27.040 --> 27:27.680
No.

291
27:28.880 --> 27:29.520
You’re overthinking it.

292
27:30.480 --> 27:31.120
Just order.

293
27:34.320 --> 27:36.200
Hey, Dean!

294
27:38.320 --> 27:39.880
Why didn’t you tell me you were coming home?

295
27:58.160 --> 28:01.080
You didn’t tell me this is your hometown,

296
28:01.400 --> 28:02.960
or that this is your big sister’s café.

297
28:04.520 --> 28:05.440
Why didn’t you say anything?

298
28:06.840 --> 28:07.880
I didn’t think it was important.

299
28:08.440 --> 28:09.120
Of course it was.

300
28:10.080 --> 28:11.960
I told you about my parents.

301
28:14.840 --> 28:16.360
You think this kind of thing isn’t important?

302
28:17.440 --> 28:19.400
It is, it is. I’m sorry.

303
28:20.000 --> 28:21.000
Wanna try this?

304
28:22.360 --> 28:23.280
No, you go ahead.

305
28:28.960 --> 28:29.760
How is everything?

306
28:30.680 --> 28:31.920
Is the drink okay?

307
28:32.520 --> 28:33.240
Yeah, it’s good.

308
28:33.680 --> 28:35.240
So, what are you guys doing here?

309
28:35.400 --> 28:36.080
Vacation?

310
28:36.560 --> 28:37.880
I’m here to do some research for work.

311
28:38.120 --> 28:40.520
I saw your café looked really nice, so we stopped by.

312
28:42.000 --> 28:44.440
But Dean didn’t tell me anything.

313
28:45.040 --> 28:45.480
What?

314
28:46.000 --> 28:48.240
Dean didn’t tell you it was my café?

315
28:49.480 --> 28:52.840
Wow. Were you trying to keep my café under wraps?

316
28:53.080 --> 28:54.160
You brat.

317
28:54.440 --> 28:55.080
Or what?

318
28:55.280 --> 28:57.160
You didn’t want your boyfriend to meet me?

319
29:03.520 --> 29:05.560
I’m just a friend. Not his boyfriend.

320
29:24.800 --> 29:25.360
What?

321
29:25.960 --> 29:27.240
Is he really not your boyfriend?

322
29:27.720 --> 29:29.160
- I told you— - Then what is he?

323
29:29.400 --> 29:30.520
A friend.

324
29:31.240 --> 29:32.160
Really.

325
29:35.560 --> 29:38.840
Be careful with your mixed signals.

326
29:39.920 --> 29:41.960
Someone else might get to him first.

327
29:46.600 --> 29:49.160
And I told Mom you’re here.

328
29:49.560 --> 29:52.160
She told me to drag you home for dinner.

329
30:10.160 --> 30:11.640
Root for me, baby girl.

330
30:19.200 --> 30:22.200
Moodeng, have you eaten yet?

331
30:22.560 --> 30:23.040
Hmm?

332
30:23.560 --> 30:24.840
Have you had some food?

333
30:26.320 --> 30:29.480
Wanna go out for a run? Hm?

334
30:31.680 --> 30:32.560
Am I right?

335
30:43.400 --> 30:44.640
Gosh, your daddy really sucks.

336
30:45.400 --> 30:46.360
What should we do?

337
30:47.440 --> 30:48.560
Should we just go home?

338
30:48.840 --> 30:49.360
Excuse me.

339
30:49.720 --> 30:51.040
Are you Mr. Monsieur?

340
30:51.160 --> 30:51.480
Yes.

341
30:51.960 --> 30:52.320
Oops.

342
30:54.880 --> 30:57.200
Holy shit.

343
30:59.160 --> 31:00.280
It’s nice to finally meet you.

344
31:02.240 --> 31:02.800
You too.

345
31:11.520 --> 31:12.080
Ten.

346
31:15.960 --> 31:16.880
You’re here too?

347
31:26.120 --> 31:26.680
Hello.

348
31:28.120 --> 31:31.480
Well, I…

349
31:34.920 --> 31:40.480
A friend of a friend of a friend who knows me invited me.

350
31:40.880 --> 31:43.000
I didn’t know I’d run into you here, Dr. Pun.

351
31:43.000 --> 31:44.120
What a coincidence.

352
31:44.560 --> 31:47.840
I thought you were someone from the chat room.

353
31:51.760 --> 31:53.480
Excuse me. I need a refill.

354
31:54.600 --> 31:55.280
Sure.

355
32:02.520 --> 32:04.400
Everyone recognizes me, girl,

356
32:04.920 --> 32:06.720
except the one person I want to recognize me.

357
32:16.120 --> 32:18.520
All right, Good Boi Friendly members,

358
32:18.520 --> 32:20.960
let’s gather around and have a chat.

359
32:21.240 --> 32:22.240
Please.

360
32:22.600 --> 32:23.320
Hey there.

361
32:24.120 --> 32:25.320
Come on in and have a seat.

362
32:25.480 --> 32:26.960
Wow, he seems to enjoy eating.

363
32:27.040 --> 32:28.240
- He likes it? - Yeah.

364
32:29.040 --> 32:29.920
I knew it.

365
32:37.520 --> 32:38.480
Alright.

366
32:38.560 --> 32:42.720
So we finally get to meet after hearing each other’s voices for so long.

367
32:42.800 --> 32:44.840
My username is Uncle Peanut Brittle.

368
32:46.720 --> 32:47.760
Next.

369
32:47.760 --> 32:49.920
My username is Truffle Pizza.

370
32:49.920 --> 32:51.000
Oh, he’s Mr. Truffle Pizza.

371
32:52.600 --> 32:54.440
My username is Mr. Hong.

372
32:54.480 --> 32:55.840
Hi, Mr. Hong.

373
32:56.280 --> 32:58.080
I’m Feeding Bowl.

374
32:58.240 --> 33:00.120
I’m Blossom.

375
33:00.160 --> 33:02.160
Ms. Blossom, it’s very nice to meet you.

376
33:02.240 --> 33:03.040
Your turn.

377
33:07.760 --> 33:08.400
I’m…

378
33:13.560 --> 33:14.600
I’m not a member of your group.

379
33:16.960 --> 33:18.880
Wait, aren’t you Mr. Monsieur?

380
33:23.920 --> 33:27.320
No, I’m Ten, not Monsieur.

381
33:27.680 --> 33:31.360
But when I called you Monsieur, you nodded.

382
33:32.760 --> 33:35.760
And your voice sounds just like Mr. Monsieur’s.

383
33:35.760 --> 33:36.680
Exactly.

384
33:36.680 --> 33:39.520
No, no, no. It’s not like that.

385
33:39.720 --> 33:42.600
I thought you called me “mister.”

386
33:43.080 --> 33:45.240
Like, “Bonjour, Monsieur.”

387
33:45.560 --> 33:46.280
Something like that.

388
33:46.280 --> 33:48.280
Come on. Where are we, Paris?

389
34:01.720 --> 34:03.760
I think everyone’s misunderstanding.

390
34:05.960 --> 34:09.239
He’s… Mr. Ten.

391
34:10.760 --> 34:12.600
I know him in real life.

392
34:14.360 --> 34:16.239
There’s no way he’s Mr. Monsieur.

393
34:18.199 --> 34:18.840
Mr. Ten, it is.

394
34:19.600 --> 34:20.760
Nice to meet you, Mr. Ten.

395
34:23.520 --> 34:25.159
Next, please.

396
34:25.159 --> 34:27.679
My username is Bagel Smoked Salmon.

397
34:27.679 --> 34:28.840
Mr. Bagel!

398
34:28.840 --> 34:31.760
Any dramatic stories to tell us today?

399
34:42.360 --> 34:43.360
Heading home already?

400
34:44.639 --> 34:45.000
Yes.

401
34:45.320 --> 34:46.320
Don’t go yet.

402
34:46.760 --> 34:47.960
Enjoy it with us a little longer.

403
34:48.159 --> 34:50.760
Besides, it’s been a while since we last met.

404
34:51.639 --> 34:52.560
I missed...

405
34:58.680 --> 34:59.160
All right.

406
35:01.400 --> 35:03.240
Aw, I missed you so much.

407
35:03.320 --> 35:05.320
Did you miss me, Mademoiselle?

408
35:06.200 --> 35:08.240
It’s been a minute, my lady.

409
35:48.800 --> 35:49.680
Come on.

410
35:50.080 --> 35:51.600
Mom finished setting the table a while ago.

411
35:52.160 --> 35:52.920
Let’s go, Moth.

412
35:58.240 --> 36:01.520
Here we go. Freshly cooked fish.

413
36:01.760 --> 36:03.680
Does it look good?

414
36:08.280 --> 36:09.600
When are you going to grow up?

415
36:11.040 --> 36:13.720
You didn’t even call to say you were coming home.

416
36:14.800 --> 36:17.600
You made your mom scramble to get everything ready.

417
36:18.920 --> 36:21.680
But I didn’t ask her to.

418
36:23.840 --> 36:25.560
It’s our family tradition.

419
36:26.880 --> 36:27.880
Dig in.

420
36:28.240 --> 36:30.760
My mom’s the best cook in the world.

421
36:32.320 --> 36:33.640
Here, Moth.

422
36:33.960 --> 36:34.560
Thank you.

423
36:34.640 --> 36:36.080
I don’t know why you have to complain.

424
36:36.160 --> 36:38.680
It’s nice that our son came home to have dinner with us.

425
36:38.720 --> 36:39.880
Moth, eat all you want.

426
36:40.000 --> 36:43.000
Dean hardly ever brings friends home.

427
36:47.360 --> 36:47.960
Yes, ma’am.

428
36:54.000 --> 36:54.680
It’s delicious.

429
36:56.480 --> 36:57.480
Mom, you eat too.

430
36:58.000 --> 36:58.880
Stop piling food on everyone’s plate.

431
37:00.160 --> 37:03.920
Moth has to eat and get back to work quickly.

432
37:04.160 --> 37:05.520
I’m not in that much of a hurry.

433
37:06.560 --> 37:08.640
I haven’t had food this good in a long time.

434
37:09.760 --> 37:13.280
But you said you’d come check the location and get back to work.

435
37:14.240 --> 37:17.080
I’m in a rush, just not as much as you are.

436
37:17.720 --> 37:19.440
Your mom’s cooking is so good. Eat.

437
37:23.640 --> 37:26.520
You know, Dean was very quiet as a kid.

438
37:26.840 --> 37:28.680
His teacher told me he didn’t talk much.

439
37:29.040 --> 37:30.680
All he did was read.

440
37:30.840 --> 37:34.680
But now, watching his videos, he seems like a completely different person.

441
37:34.760 --> 37:36.000
He’s so talkative.

442
37:37.640 --> 37:38.560
That’s interesting.

443
37:39.240 --> 37:40.480
I never knew this side of him.

444
37:42.680 --> 37:43.440
Mom.

445
37:44.240 --> 37:45.840
Don’t show him my old photos.

446
37:45.920 --> 37:46.760
And why would you tell him that?

447
37:48.120 --> 37:48.920
Moth, look at this.

448
37:49.120 --> 37:50.720
Dean in glasses.

449
37:50.760 --> 37:52.000
Look at that round face.

450
37:53.120 --> 37:56.720
Dean doesn’t tell me much about his life.

451
37:57.440 --> 37:59.440
How is he in Bangkok?

452
37:59.560 --> 38:01.160
Does he have lots of friends?

453
38:02.320 --> 38:05.640
Well, yes, he does.

454
38:07.160 --> 38:08.280
A lot, indeed.

455
38:09.040 --> 38:10.080
That’s great.

456
38:10.120 --> 38:13.120
Next time, bring your friends home with you.

457
38:14.240 --> 38:15.080
Come on, Mom.

458
38:15.400 --> 38:16.360
My friend has to go back now.

459
38:17.200 --> 38:18.240
He’s got work.

460
38:18.520 --> 38:20.880
What? You’re not staying the night?

461
38:21.960 --> 38:23.200
Can you stay one night?

462
38:26.120 --> 38:27.480
We can’t this time.

463
38:28.840 --> 38:29.920
Deadline’s pretty tight.

464
38:37.960 --> 38:39.480
Here, take this with you.

465
38:40.800 --> 38:42.720
Wow, it’s a lot. I can’t finish all this.

466
38:44.040 --> 38:45.760
Come here. Give me a hug.

467
38:45.880 --> 38:47.040
All right.

468
38:48.840 --> 38:50.280
Drive safe.

469
38:50.400 --> 38:52.440
Get back to Bangkok safe and sound.

470
38:52.720 --> 38:54.760
And if you have time, come home for a visit.

471
38:54.960 --> 38:56.560
If I get the chance, I will.

472
38:57.200 --> 38:59.200
That’s what you always say.

473
38:59.400 --> 39:01.720
Get going. Let me know when you get to Bangkok.

474
39:01.840 --> 39:02.560
Sure, Mom.

475
39:02.720 --> 39:03.320
Let me have a kiss.

476
39:05.720 --> 39:06.360
See you.

477
39:09.240 --> 39:10.760
Goodbye, ma’am.

478
39:11.440 --> 39:12.280
Thank you for the food.

479
39:14.480 --> 39:17.520
I should be thanking you, Moth.

480
39:18.360 --> 39:19.720
Please take care of Dean.

481
39:20.320 --> 39:24.000
He lives alone in Bangkok and never tells us anything.

482
39:24.320 --> 39:27.600
But knowing he has you with him puts my mind at ease.

483
39:30.320 --> 39:30.800
Yes, ma’am.

484
39:33.240 --> 39:34.120
Let’s go already.

485
39:36.280 --> 39:36.920
Bye now.

486
39:37.760 --> 39:38.480
See you, Mom.

487
39:41.120 --> 39:42.200
Come visit again.

488
40:02.680 --> 40:04.200
(Mr. Monsieur has joined us.)

489
40:04.480 --> 40:05.880
(Where did you go today?)

490
40:11.720 --> 40:12.440
I…

491
40:14.160 --> 40:15.920
I was sick. That’s why I didn’t show up.

492
40:16.560 --> 40:17.720
(You really weren’t there?)

493
40:17.760 --> 40:20.200
(Someone claimed to be Monsieur today.)

494
40:20.840 --> 40:21.880
I really wasn’t there.

495
40:22.440 --> 40:24.680
Maybe he misunderstood and thought you greeted him in French.

496
40:24.720 --> 40:29.200
(Hold on. You didn’t go, but you sure sound like you knew what happened.)

497
40:30.760 --> 40:32.680
Sorry, I’m late.

498
40:33.560 --> 40:35.240
It’s good you’re here, Mr. Bagel.

499
40:35.720 --> 40:37.680
What are we talking about today?

500
40:38.760 --> 40:42.640
Before we start, have something to tell you guys.

501
40:43.520 --> 40:47.560
From now on, I won’t have time to come online and chat with you.

502
40:53.040 --> 40:58.080
I’ll be very busy with work and personal stuff.

503
41:00.360 --> 41:05.680
I didn’t tell you all at the event today because I was afraid you’d be sad.

504
41:07.920 --> 41:14.200
Even if I’m no longer on this app, you can still come see me at my clinic.

505
41:14.640 --> 41:17.040
(Wait! Mr. Bagel, are you a doctor?)

506
41:17.800 --> 41:21.520
That’s right. My name is Pun,

507
41:21.520 --> 41:23.000
and I’m a veterinarian.

508
41:23.200 --> 41:25.200
I run a clinic called Buddy Heal.

509
41:26.120 --> 41:29.440
If you see me, come say hi.

510
41:29.600 --> 41:32.680
(What a shame. I won’t get to hear your voice anymore, Mr. Bagel.)

511
41:32.760 --> 41:33.280
(Exactly.)

512
41:33.720 --> 41:35.560
(Hey, we should call him Dr. Pun now.)

513
41:37.440 --> 41:38.160
Dr. Pun!

514
41:40.520 --> 41:40.960
Yes?

515
41:41.440 --> 41:42.560
Wait for me.

516
41:43.160 --> 41:44.440
I’m coming to see you at the clinic.

517
41:47.760 --> 41:50.960
If you are, you’d better head out now.

518
41:52.960 --> 41:55.640
We close at nine.

519
41:57.640 --> 41:58.600
8:30 PM

520
41:58.600 --> 41:59.440
Shit.

521
42:04.640 --> 42:06.240
(Hey, do you hear someone running?)

522
42:06.240 --> 42:07.360
(Mr. Monsieur?)

523
42:07.840 --> 42:09.640
(Go say goodbye to Mr. Bagel before he leaves.)

524
42:12.800 --> 42:15.320
(The roads to Dr. Pun’s clinic are all red on the map.)

525
42:16.240 --> 42:18.120
(Whoa. Traffic is horrible today.)

526
42:19.880 --> 42:21.520
(Will Mr. Monsieur make it in time?)

527
42:21.880 --> 42:23.000
8:45 PM

528
42:23.000 --> 42:24.320
Mr. Bagel, traffic is completely jammed.

529
42:24.760 --> 42:25.640
Please wait for me.

530
42:25.640 --> 42:27.760
8:45 PM

531
42:43.240 --> 42:44.360
(I’m helping you find a way.)

532
42:44.840 --> 42:45.680
Damn it, the traffic.

533
42:45.680 --> 42:47.400
(There’s a small alley behind the market.)

534
42:48.040 --> 42:52.120
Bro, go behind the market. In there. Go!

535
42:53.880 --> 42:55.120
8:55 PM

536
42:57.240 --> 42:58.520
(The road in front of the clinic is jammed.)

537
42:58.520 --> 42:59.400
(You’d better use the one behind it.)

538
42:59.400 --> 43:01.880
Bro, this alley. Turn here.

539
43:02.880 --> 43:04.280
8:58 PM

540
43:09.840 --> 43:12.360
Bro, stop right here at the minimart.

541
43:15.280 --> 43:16.800
Here. No change.

542
43:25.400 --> 43:26.600
[OPEN DAILY FROM 9 A.M. TO 9 P.M.]

543
43:28.960 --> 43:31.960
(Mr. Monsieur, did you make it before Mr. Bagel left?)

544
43:32.920 --> 43:35.480
(I don’t think he did.)

545
43:47.680 --> 43:50.680
Dr. Pun, please come out to see me.

546
43:51.040 --> 43:51.520
Yes.

547
44:12.680 --> 44:16.440
Dr. Pun, if I confess something,

548
44:17.680 --> 44:19.240
please don’t be mad at me.

549
44:24.360 --> 44:25.200
I’m…

550
44:33.080 --> 44:34.320
I’m Monsieur.

551
44:44.200 --> 44:47.840
Ah. I already knew that.

552
45:08.600 --> 45:12.200
I thought you were someone from the chat room.

553
45:15.040 --> 45:17.160
My name is Ten, not Monsieur.

554
45:18.800 --> 45:21.480
Hello. I’m Long Arm T-Rex.

555
45:23.840 --> 45:26.840
Is there anything you want to tell me, Mr. Monsieur?

556
45:28.880 --> 45:29.920
There isn’t.

557
45:34.080 --> 45:35.760
[GENTLE FOX]

558
45:35.760 --> 45:37.320
The day we went to the blind date event,

559
45:38.080 --> 45:41.800
I already knew you were Long Arm T-Rex.

560
45:42.960 --> 45:44.400
You knew that day?

561
45:44.800 --> 45:45.560
No.

562
45:46.520 --> 45:47.920
I’ve known all along,

563
45:48.280 --> 45:50.520
and I couldn’t help feeling disappointed.

564
45:52.200 --> 45:56.920
I thought you were going to tell me that you were Monsieur.

565
45:59.040 --> 46:05.360
Dr. Pun, aren’t you mad that I hid it from you?

566
46:07.280 --> 46:08.880
And that I…

567
46:11.040 --> 46:13.320
lied to you so many times?

568
46:14.040 --> 46:17.560
I kind of understand why you did it.

569
46:19.000 --> 46:25.600
But at least today, I’m glad you finally had the courage to come see me.

570
46:45.760 --> 46:46.600
So…

571
46:48.640 --> 46:50.600
Now that we’ve revealed our real identities,

572
46:53.000 --> 46:56.440
how about we start going out?

573
47:08.680 --> 47:11.480
♪ I want your love, so I gave you mine ♪

574
47:11.560 --> 47:14.280
♪ The love is clear in every sign ♪

575
47:14.280 --> 47:16.720
♪ What’s your answer, will you approve? ♪

576
47:16.720 --> 47:20.160
♪ Will you admit you love me too? ♪

577
47:20.200 --> 47:22.800
♪ There’s nothing I wouldn’t do ♪

578
47:22.800 --> 47:25.320
♪ Every bit of my heart belongs to you ♪

579
47:25.320 --> 47:27.400
♪ Giving you love, hoping you’ll reciprocate ♪

580
47:27.640 --> 47:31.040
♪ So tell me, are we on the same page? ♪

581
47:35.600 --> 47:39.320
♪ So tell me, are we on the same page? ♪

582
47:46.760 --> 47:48.240
Can I crash at your place tonight?

583
47:51.880 --> 47:53.040
You should go home tonight.

584
47:56.760 --> 47:57.480
I’m sorry.

585
47:58.800 --> 47:59.280
Huh?

586
48:01.680 --> 48:03.280
Did I make you uncomfortable?

587
48:04.960 --> 48:06.360
Why would I be uncomfortable?

588
48:07.400 --> 48:10.000
Duen even asked to follow you on Instagram.

589
48:10.800 --> 48:11.880
You didn’t have to accept her request.

590
48:13.120 --> 48:14.240
Why would I reject it?

591
48:16.120 --> 48:18.000
It’s just being friends on IG.

592
48:18.520 --> 48:19.640
And your sister is pretty lovely.

593
48:22.000 --> 48:24.600
But you don’t usually accept just anyone’s requests.

594
48:25.240 --> 48:27.360
Why can’t I be friends with her?

595
48:28.920 --> 48:30.240
Your family members are pretty nice.

596
48:31.440 --> 48:35.360
You’re the only one who seems like you don’t want to talk to them.

597
48:39.480 --> 48:44.560
And you’re okay with them thinking we’re together?

598
48:46.640 --> 48:47.720
Um…

599
48:49.480 --> 48:52.560
It doesn’t bother me if they think that.

600
48:56.160 --> 48:56.720
I’m getting off.

601
49:12.920 --> 49:16.040
Be careful with your mixed signals.

602
49:16.880 --> 49:18.840
Someone else might get to him first.

603
49:32.600 --> 49:33.120
Moth.

604
49:52.320 --> 49:55.080
Why don’t we try… getting together?

605
50:45.360 --> 50:46.000
Moth.

606
50:49.520 --> 50:50.880
You’re still the same.

607
50:51.040 --> 50:53.520
Do you know a guy named Mes?

608
50:53.840 --> 50:54.880
So you’ve met him?

609
50:55.320 --> 50:56.440
Yeah, big time.

610
50:56.840 --> 50:58.480
You’re still so precise with your colors.

611
50:58.560 --> 51:00.480
I just painted the way my feelings told me to.

612
51:01.000 --> 51:02.080
Just like you.

613
51:02.520 --> 51:04.640
Moth, will you start painting again?

614
51:05.160 --> 51:07.360
Give me a chance to see your work again.

615
51:07.680 --> 51:09.400
Why don’t you tell him and get it over with?

616
51:09.400 --> 51:10.720
Tell him you like him.

617
51:10.720 --> 51:11.600
Are you drunk?

618
51:11.600 --> 51:12.280
Drunk?

619
51:12.680 --> 51:13.480
Are you jealous?
